  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1256 PM CDT Fri May 22 2026\n\nOur unsettled weather pattern will remain in place into the middle \nof next week. Right now Sunday looks like convection will be \ndiurnally driven with storms in the afternoon and evening and mainly \nover the eastern half of the area. Our airmass will be about the \nsame and locally heavy rain will continue to be possible. Monday is \nlooking like a mostly dry day with only low chance POPs over our \neastern counties. The next significant shortwave will move across \nTexas Tuesday into Wednesday bringing another round of showers and \nthunderstorms. PW will again be 1.5+\" and locally heavy rain will be \npossible. Showers and thunderstorms will linger over the east on \nThursday.",
